+// An imported alias can deliberately preserve one host ABI carrier for a source union whose web
+// alternatives collapse at the native boundary.  When that exact alias is passed back to the same
+// source union (Canvas drawImage/createPattern are the motivating APIs), contextual union construction
+// must not reopen the alias and try to reconstruct alternatives the host carrier cannot distinguish.
+// Both sides are required to expand to the identical source union, so this is an alias erasure rather
+// than a widening or an unchecked selection.
+function isCppExactImportedAliasCarrierArgumentCpp(
+  expression: Readonly<IrExpression>,
+  expectedType: Readonly<IrType>,
+  context: EmitContext,
+): boolean {
